# Read by GitHub ("Cite this repository") and by Zenodo, which takes the
# authors from here for the DOI of each published release. `version` is
# rewritten by `cz bump` (version_files in pyproject.toml).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use kennis in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: kennis
version: 0.13.1
abstract: >-
  kennis is a local knowledge and memory system for people and AI agents. It
  holds papers, documentation sites and notes in a corpus under git, searches
  them by keywords and by meaning, and serves them to agents over MCP, with
  citations that link each claim to the passage it rests on.
authors:
  - family-names: Welman
    given-names: Brian
repository-code: "https://github.com/kwazzi-jack/kennis"
url: "https://kwazzi-jack.github.io/kennis/"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - knowledge base
  - retrieval
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - citations
  - MCP
  - research software
